@*
  The way on (T350, flow 04; round 1, Q6 and correction d; round 2, C1, C10 d; R3-C-Activity; DESIGN.md § Page-level
  patterns, "Record page with a workflow", R3): straight after a move's result on the activity page, outside its live
  region, which holds only the result's sentence and what is left ("Completed. 1 more waits for you.").
  - Something still waits: the next row (WaitingList's, with since when), "Open the next", named for its item, and
    "Back to" the acting role's list by the owner table (NavOwners.OwnerFor), else "Back to Home".
  - Nothing left: "Go to Home".
  No automatic advance (Q6). The row's link is out of the tab order, so the next Tab after the focused result is "Open
  the next" (C10 d); a pointer and a screen reader's browse mode still have it.
*@
@if (Next is { } next)
{
  <section class="way-on" aria-label="The next activity waiting for you">
    <WaitingList Items="@([next])" WithSince="true" LinksOutOfTabOrder="true" />
    <div class="form-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/activities/@next.Id" aria-label="@OpenLabel(next)">Open the next</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="@BackHref">@BackLabel</a>
    </div>
  </section>
}
else
{
  <p class="way-on-none"><a class="btn btn-outline" href="@HomeHref">Go to Home</a></p>
}

@code {
  /// <summary>The first row still waiting for the reader, the activity just moved left out; null when nothing waits.</summary>
  [Parameter] public ActivitySummaryDto? Next { get; set; }

  /// <summary>"Back to Activity inbox": the acting role's list the page is under (the owner table), else "Back to Home".</summary>
  [Parameter] public string BackLabel { get; set; } = "Back to Home";

  [Parameter] public string BackHref { get; set; } = HomeHref;

  private const string HomeHref = "/";

  /// <summary>"Open the next: Mini-CEX (Paediatrics) · PAED-001 · 2026-09-20, from Anele Dlamini" (Spec § 3).</summary>
  public static string OpenLabel(ActivitySummaryDto next) => $"Open the next: {ActivityRowNames.WaitingLinkWords(next)}";
}
